-- ============================================================================
-- 27 - Navigation
-- ============================================================================
-- The single owner of the menu, and the last file to apply.
--
-- It used to be written by four files — 05, 11, 16 and 22 — each carrying the
-- menu as it stood when that slice was built. Applying the whole set in order
-- worked, because the last writer won. Applying any one of them on its own
-- silently reverted the menu to an older shape, which this project hit twice
-- before recognising the pattern. Navigation is page-spanning state, so it
-- belongs to one file that runs after every page it names exists.
--
-- Icons: `ICON` takes a model reference into an icon collection, not a string,
-- so an unknown name is rejected rather than written through. Hyphenated Atlas
-- names must be double-quoted. Browse them with
-- `DESCRIBE ICON COLLECTION Atlas_Core.Atlas` (366 icons).
--
-- Two of these are not the icons Studio Pro originally had. `ICON` reaches
-- Forms$IconCollectionIcon only; Accounts carried a Forms$GlyphIcon (numeric
-- code 9999) and Categories & rules a Forms$ImageIcon (System.Images.Close),
-- and MDL can express neither — DESCRIBE now names them in a comment rather
-- than dropping them in silence (FINDINGS 81). Both were placeholders, so they
-- are authored here as collection icons that mean something, which is what
-- keeps this file reproducible.
-- ============================================================================

create or replace navigation Responsive
  home page Ledger.Dashboard
  menu (
    menu item 'Dashboard' page Ledger.Dashboard icon Atlas_Core.Atlas."align-center";
    menu item 'Cashflow' page Ledger.Cashflow_Overview icon Atlas_Core.Atlas."align-bottom";
    menu item 'Budgets' page Ledger.Budgets_Overview icon Atlas_Core.Atlas_Filled."alert-circle";
    menu item 'Insights' page Ledger.Insights icon Atlas_Core.Atlas."analytics-graph-bar";
    -- Atlas_Styling, not Atlas: a different collection with a different CSS
    -- prefix (Atlas_Core_Controls rather than mx-icon). It renders, but Atlas'
    -- navigation styling matches on .glyphicon/.mx-icon-lined/.mx-icon-filled,
    -- so this one was skipped by every nav rule — including the one that gives
    -- the glyph its width in a collapsed sidebar. The result was one menu item
    -- whose caption stayed visible when the rest were pushed out of view.
    menu item 'Transactions' page Ledger.Transaction_Overview icon Atlas_Core.Atlas."cash-payment-bill";
    menu item 'Import' page Ledger.Import_Overview icon Atlas_Core.Atlas."download-bottom";
    -- was a glyph icon (code 9999), which MDL cannot express
    menu item 'Accounts' page Ledger.Account_Overview icon Atlas_Core.Atlas."credit-card";
    -- was System.Images.Close, an image icon, which MDL cannot express
    menu item 'Categories & rules' page Ledger.Category_Overview icon Atlas_Core.Atlas."tag-group";
  );
/
